+//! The rules of the log, as values: terms, entries, a majority, and when an entry may be called
+//! committed.
+//!
+//! `meshkv/5.2-replication-rules` is an *aware* step: its subject is the handful of rules every
+//! consensus protocol is built out of, and its deliverable is that they exist here as values with
+//! refusals — not as a paragraph the next reader is hoped to remember. The network that carries
+//! these values between nodes is `5.3`'s.
+
+use crate::error::Result;
+
+/// A position in the log: one-based, monotonic, never reused.
+pub type Index = u64;
+
+/// How many elections the cluster has been through.
+///
+/// A term moves in one direction only — up — and every message from `5.3` on carries the sender's
+/// term. A node that sees a higher term is behind, not ahead, and that is the whole reason terms
+/// exist: they order events that happened at nodes which cannot see each other.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Hash)]
+pub struct Term(u64);
+
